{
  "//": [
    "frisian-mcp demo — NetBox host.",
    "",
    "Merge the mcpServers block below into your MCP client's configuration.",
    "The tokens are real and work exactly as printed: they are fixed, published",
    "demo constants baked into the demo images, not placeholders to substitute.",
    "",
    "Three entries, because the demo IS the difference between them. Connect all",
    "three and compare what each one lists.",
    "",
    "THIS HOST IS THE ONE WITH THREE SEPARATE DOORS. On Nautobot and Paperless",
    "the three entries differ only by the TOKEN — one mount point, three",
    "identities. Here the URLs differ too: FRISIAN_MCP_ROUTES puts a tier",
    "ceiling on each path, so the door limits what ANY caller can reach and the",
    "identity narrows it further. Point the admin token at the read-only URL and",
    "it gets list and retrieve, nothing else. That combination is the thing this",
    "host exists to show, and it is worth trying on purpose.",
    "",
    "The port is 8083. Nautobot uses 8080, Paperless 8081, Open edX 8082, so all",
    "of them can run at once.",
    "",
    "THE ADMIN DOOR IS /api/mcp/ops, NOT /api/mcp/admin. MCP clients strip an",
    "`admin` suffix and retry the bare URL, which lands the caller on a",
    "different route with a different tier ceiling — silently. Do not tidy the",
    "path."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "netbox-read-only": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8083/api/mcp/read-only",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer frisian-demo-readonly-token-public-do-not-reuse"
      }
    },
    "netbox-read-write": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8083/api/mcp/read-write",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer frisian-demo-netops-token-public-do-not-reuse"
      }
    },
    "netbox-ops": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8083/api/mcp/ops",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer frisian-demo-admin-token-public-do-not-reuse"
      }
    }
  }
}
